  "refinements": [
    "The site plan was a circulation plan, not a narrow-corridor token master. Main circulation is widened to 3.2–3.6m in this proposal; original room footprints/levels remain.",
    "The lower workshop stair opens directly off the covered service passage, before the pier.",
    "The records stair branches north from the hub. A separate south corridor bends into the guard bay just outside the locked inspection door.",
    "The spare records desk faces east along the west side. Turn left from the stair into the deeper pocket behind the crates at its south end.",
    "The platform return flight stays west of the inspection gallery wall and joins the inner post. It does not cut diagonally through that wall.",
    "The signal platform extends two metres east. The crosswalk passes the guard stair’s sightline; the solid stair cheek screens the operating position farther east.",
    "The west wall holds the wax stove below the work window, then the press and stamp chest. A low shelf holds empty trays beside the wash-yard door.",
    "The workshop stair opens onto a lamplit crossing. Wait for both seal workers to face the press, then cross to the east side of the south cooling rack.",
    "The workshop descent and platform return have a solid divider. There is no new hub-to-platform doorway.",
    "The court stance moves 0.4m south within the existing court to fit the phone marker. Court footprint remains 22.5,21 / 7×3m.",
    "Portals change crop at a landing; room and hub crops share the same metre-space handoff point. Passage art beyond a seam is context, not an extra selectable room."
  ],
